From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:05:05 -0400
Subject: Always robust init all levels of immutable textures

A previous change made it such that only BASE+ levels are
robust-initialized.  This is fine for mutable textures, since levels
outside this range are inaccessible to GL.  However, that's not true for
immutable textures, where framebuffer completeness is always true
regardless of which level the framebuffer is attached to.

Bug: chromium:553117511
Change-Id: Ied52d392f79bed56152c063816be2986b810080f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8415406
Reviewed-by: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): this ANGLE revision predates the
EnsureInitializedLevels parameter of Texture::ensureInitialized, so the
BaseOnly handling has no counterpart here; the fix is applied to the
single-mode function (initFirstLevel = 0 for immutable textures, base
level otherwise). Test-only hunks (expectations, CopyTextureTest,
RobustResourceInitTest) were dropped because they did not apply.

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/Texture.cpp b/src/libANGLE/Texture.cpp
index 201d8955105036d6682d47cfc7f399ab8c375bf1..1d6ea0a03ac678583ffccb723e288f6840337a68 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/Texture.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/Texture.cpp
@@ -2529,12 +2529,18 @@ angle::Result Texture::ensureInitialized(const Context *context)
         return angle::Result::Continue;
     }
 
-    bool anyDirty = false;
-    bool allInitialized = (mState.getEffectiveBaseLevel() == 0);
+    const GLint baseLevel = mState.getEffectiveBaseLevel();
+    // Start initializing from baseLevel if the texture is mutable.  If the texture is immutable,
+    // initialize all the levels because framebuffers outside [BASE, MAX] range are complete for
+    // immutable textures.
+    const GLint initFirstLevel = !getImmutableFormat() ? baseLevel : 0;
+
+    bool anyDirty       = false;
+    bool allInitialized = (initFirstLevel == 0);
 
     ImageIndexIterator it = ImageIndexIterator::MakeGeneric(
-        mState.mType, static_cast<GLint>(mState.getEffectiveBaseLevel()),
-        IMPLEMENTATION_MAX_TEXTURE_LEVELS + 1, ImageIndex::kEntireLevel, ImageIndex::kEntireLevel);
+        mState.mType, initFirstLevel, IMPLEMENTATION_MAX_TEXTURE_LEVELS + 1,
+        ImageIndex::kEntireLevel, ImageIndex::kEntireLevel);
     while (it.hasNext())
     {
         const ImageIndex index = it.next();
